    "sections": [
      {
        "discipline": "OVERVIEW",
        "title": "What it is",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "pb4817fbca4c4.1",
            "text": "Leather is used for clothing, footwear, handbags, furniture, tools and sports equipment, and finished leather is fashioned into shoes and boots, belts, upholstery, saddles, gloves, luggage and purses.",
            "level": "PROVISIONAL",
            "claimIds": [
              "852cafa2-a62b-50c3-ab6e-0af34744ff35",
              "bc2820fa-2482-57dd-a30c-2836f04ad9b5"
            ],
            "terms": [],
            "subCategories": [],
            "crafts": []
          },
          {
            "id": "pb4817fbca4c4.2",
            "text": "Leathers are traditionally made by vegetable, chrome and syntan tanning, though newer sustainable methods have since been developed.",
            "level": "PROVISIONAL",
            "claimIds": [
              "92216fa7-cc46-5a36-8b2e-51c9ecdd8e6d"
            ],
            "terms": [],
            "subCategories": [],
            "crafts": []
          },
          {
            "id": "pb4817fbca4c4.3",
            "text": "Among footwear, Kolhapuri chappals are handmade open footwear made of vegetable-tanned leather with traditional techniques and tools.",
            "level": "PROVISIONAL",
            "claimIds": [
              "d5b92396-9e80-55b7-a9e3-5149d460814e"
            ],
            "terms": [],
            "subCategories": [
              "Leather-Footwear"
            ],
            "crafts": [
              "Kolhapuri-Chappal"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "pb4817fbca4c4.4",
            "text": "Among other articles, Kanpur Saddlery craftsmen make saddles, harnesses and other equestrian equipment from leather obtained from local tanneries, and Santiniketan leather goods are a byproduct of Rabindranath Tagore's Rural Reconstruction initiative at Visva-Bharati University.",
            "level": "PROVISIONAL",
            "claimIds": [
              "a3c39395-7f6e-5e2c-90ef-177fae6912fe",
              "006c72f8-9024-5bf2-8513-c64c3924db0a"
            ],
            "terms": [],
            "subCategories": [
              "Leather-Other-Articles"
            ],
            "crafts": [
              "Kanpur-Saddlery",
              "Santiniketan-Leather-Goods"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "pb4817fbca4c4.5",
            "text": "Tholu bommalata, literally the dance of the leather puppets, is the shadow theatre tradition of Andhra Pradesh, Telangana and part of Karnataka, and togalu gombeyata is a traditional shadow theatre of Karnataka.",
            "level": "PROVISIONAL",
            "claimIds": [
              "c729d5cb-745c-5e94-a4be-a2c04830e00f",
              "96b58cc2-6f9f-5eb8-a25a-034d3ee3c5b1"
            ],
            "terms": [
              {
                "text": "Tholu bommalata",
                "termKey": "tholu-bommalata"
              },
              {
                "text": "togalu gombeyata",
                "termKey": "togalu-gombeyata"
              }
            ],
            "subCategories": [
              "Leather-Other-Articles"
            ],
            "crafts": [
              "Andhra-Pradesh-Leather-Puppetry"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
