    {
      "id": "b67a7053-21da-5a82-a894-01e83820f989",
      "text": "Chamar names a widespread caste of northern India whose hereditary occupation is tanning leather, from the Sanskrit charmakara, skin worker.",
      "level": "PROVISIONAL",
      "discipline": "OVERVIEW",
      "sourcesDiffer": false,
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "ea1b0d2a-d8ef-5e3d-b065-f54360b1a936",
          "claimId": "b67a7053-21da-5a82-a894-01e83820f989",
          "sourceId": "37cc4446-9121-5f45-8b5d-3c083dde91d8",
          "quote": "widespreadcaste in northern India whose hereditary occupation is tanning leather; the name is derived from the Sanskrit word charmakara (\"skin worker\").",
          "locator": "entry",
          "context": null,
          "evidence": "QUOTED",
          "level": "PROVISIONAL"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6db3e223-90e4-5c13-a142-31e0efc8cd12",
      "text": "In the Kolhapuri trade the Dhors run the tanneries and the Chambhars make the chappals by hand.",
      "level": "PROVISIONAL",
      "discipline": "OVERVIEW",
      "sourcesDiffer": false,
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "74898e31-3390-5168-b8b3-10324e53dc6f",
          "claimId": "6db3e223-90e4-5c13-a142-31e0efc8cd12",
          "sourceId": "36a0b4bf-b047-5c90-a5b8-e2dd43459f8b",
          "quote": "The Dhors, to which Vathkar belongs, run the tanneries, and the Chambhars make the chappals by hand.",
          "locator": "para. 7",
          "context": null,
          "evidence": "QUOTED",
          "level": "PROVISIONAL"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "92216fa7-cc46-5a36-8b2e-51c9ecdd8e6d",
      "text": "Leathers are traditionally made by three types of tanning, vegetable, chrome and syntan tanning, though newer sustainable methods have since been developed.",
      "level": "PROVISIONAL",
      "discipline": "OVERVIEW",
      "sourcesDiffer": false,
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "c220d621-3b44-52da-8fb4-a1d30f40e03b",
          "claimId": "92216fa7-cc46-5a36-8b2e-51c9ecdd8e6d",
          "sourceId": "21a074d3-69da-54dd-9e0d-eca64e5d8daa",
          "quote": "Traditionally, leathers are processed by the three types of tanning methods including vegetable tanning, chrome tanning and syntan tanning but recently the tanning processes are quite improved with the development of various sustainable tanning methods.",
          "locator": "section 6.2, Tanning methods",
          "context": null,
          "evidence": "QUOTED",
          "level": "PROVISIONAL"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bc2820fa-2482-57dd-a30c-2836f04ad9b5",
      "text": "Finished leather is fashioned into shoes and boots, apparel, belts, upholstery, suede goods, saddles, gloves, luggage, purses and recreational equipment.",
      "level": "PROVISIONAL",
      "discipline": "OVERVIEW",
      "sourcesDiffer": false,
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "90d80a21-b7d4-5f59-8c62-b774a2168041",
          "claimId": "bc2820fa-2482-57dd-a30c-2836f04ad9b5",
          "sourceId": "45c6bcdc-3d1e-5d21-b8f2-a0f35380157c",
          "quote": "The leather is then ready to be fashioned into any of a multitude of products. These include shoes and boots, outer apparel, belts, upholstery materials, suede products, saddles, gloves, luggage and purses, and recreational equipment",
          "locator": "Modern leather making",
          "context": null,
          "evidence": "QUOTED",
          "level": "PROVISIONAL"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5b94d767-0b1a-5934-9584-c76ca35b34b2",
      "text": "A study published in 2025 puts approximately 3,000 tanneries along the Ganga and a cluster of around 400 in Jajmau, Kanpur.",
      "level": "PROVISIONAL",
      "discipline": "GEOGRAPHY",
      "sourcesDiffer": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "0b412a96-4473-54ad-94bf-6a650aee5908",
          "claimId": "5b94d767-0b1a-5934-9584-c76ca35b34b2",
