    {
      "id": "d2ba5754-7c2e-5770-9142-7d1194dd38b5",
      "text": "Santiniketan leather goods are made from vegetable-tanned sheep and goat skins, which retain embossed imprints permanently.",
      "level": "PROVISIONAL",
      "discipline": "MATERIALS",
      "sourcesDiffer": false,
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "b7252474-2baf-5f9f-a1cf-9e4ff398cdde",
          "claimId": "d2ba5754-7c2e-5770-9142-7d1194dd38b5",
          "sourceId": "9b33be6e-51de-5c74-bc92-86b21cd9ffad",
          "quote": "Such vegetable-tanned leather pieces retain embossed imprints permanently, making them an ideal raw material for this craft. The leather pieces come from sheep and goat skins.",
          "locator": "Legacy of the Leather",
          "context": null,
          "evidence": "QUOTED",
          "level": "PROVISIONAL"
        },
        {
          "id": "d01828b1-188d-549e-93c6-ec183a94fe01",
          "claimId": "d2ba5754-7c2e-5770-9142-7d1194dd38b5",
          "sourceId": "d9593d46-3ef6-5b30-974b-68fedb0249ea",
          "quote": "trays, and domestic objects-made from vegetable-tanned goat and sheepskin and decorated through embossing, stencil work, and batik techniques",
          "locator": "para. 3",
          "context": null,
          "evidence": "QUOTED",
          "level": "PROVISIONAL"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "17ad6bab-9c40-5a8b-8646-9cbb685b6110",
      "text": "Shadow theatre probably spread from South India to South East Asia and beyond during that period, with local styles developing from Indonesia to China.",
      "level": "HYPOTHESIS",
      "discipline": "HISTORY",
      "sourcesDiffer": false,
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "85858a39-2d72-5a8a-ba46-e20ece813e0b",
          "claimId": "17ad6bab-9c40-5a8b-8646-9cbb685b6110",
          "sourceId": "b06ea566-d456-5676-9b88-4b43a3e52b9a",
          "quote": "It is probably during this period that shadow theatre from South India spread to South East Asia and beyond, and local styles developed in Indonesia, Burma, Thailand, Malaysia, Japan and China.",
          "locator": "Introduction, para. 4",
          "context": null,
          "evidence": "QUOTED",
          "level": "HYPOTHESIS"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3825018f-793e-5994-bf44-48264a264c96",
      "text": "Shadow puppetry in South India was already popular under the Satavahana and Chalukya dynasties, which Sahapedia dates to the 4th to 6th centuries AD.",
      "level": "PROVISIONAL",
      "discipline": "HISTORY",
      "sourcesDiffer": false,
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "7015cd69-a45c-508f-b10e-134348208e8e",
          "claimId": "3825018f-793e-5994-bf44-48264a264c96",
          "sourceId": "b06ea566-d456-5676-9b88-4b43a3e52b9a",
          "quote": "Shadow puppetry in South India has a very long history-it was indeed already popular under Satavahana and Chalukya dynasties (4th - 6th centuries AD).",
          "locator": "Introduction, para. 4",
          "context": null,
          "evidence": "QUOTED",
          "level": "PROVISIONAL"
        }
      ]
